post_install() {
    cat <<'AURGEN_MESSAGES'
lightXDM is installed, but nothing is set up yet. As your regular user, run: lightxdm-install
It asks for sudo, installs the packages of your desktop and sets up the TTY1 login (lightxdm-install --help).
AURGEN_MESSAGES
}

post_upgrade() {
    cat <<'AURGEN_MESSAGES'
lightXDM was updated. To apply the new version, each user who set it up runs: lightxdm-update
AURGEN_MESSAGES
}

pre_remove() {
    cat <<'AURGEN_MESSAGES'
Removing this package does not undo the lightXDM setup: run sudo lightxdm-uninstall before removing it.
If the package is already removed, reinstall it to get lightxdm-uninstall back.
AURGEN_MESSAGES
}

